oxed
====

An ed-first terminal editor written in OxCaml.

DESCRIPTION

    oxed combines traditional ed commands with Unicode editing,
    keyboard and mouse interaction, Tree-sitter, and LSP.

    All editing interfaces share a common transaction engine.

IMPLEMENTATION

    OxCaml       Language and runtime
    Zed          Text buffers and editing
    Lambda-term  Terminal interface
    Lwt          Asynchronous operations
    Tree-sitter  Syntax analysis (planned)
    LSP          Language services (planned)

BUILD

    eval "$(opam env --switch=oxcaml --set-switch)"
    dune build

TEST

    dune exec ./test/terminal_smoke.exe
    dune exec ./test/terminal_smoke.exe -- fail

STATUS

    Experimental. Application skeleton compiles.
    Terminal lifecycle tests pass.
    Editing and language services remain unfinished.

DEVELOPMENT

    Compiler-driven, interface-first development.
    Each implementation follows a verified diagnostic.

DOCUMENTATION

    SPEC       Software requirements
    CHANGELOG  Development history and verification
